url: "https://huggingface.co/spaces/immu4989/lurescope"
abstract: >-
  LureScope safely triages RFC 5322 email, scores fraud-lure likelihood, applies
  adversarial attacks, and tests an input-normalization defense. LureProof adds a
  strict, privacy-minimized evidence artifact containing detector and threshold
  provenance plus attack and defense outcomes without message content. A standard
  DSSE envelope can authenticate the statement against an external trust key.
  The inbox workflow turns reported-email queues into minimized routing manifests,
  per-case proofs, and offline SIEM payloads. Shadow Inbox and Pilot Gate measure a
  registered email control before enforcement, while the Federal Email Assurance
  Profile exports aggregate NIST OSCAL 1.2.2 assessment observations. LureEval
  adds signed, privacy-minimized cross-organization operational receipts; the
  Microsoft Defender importer enables offline paired evaluation; and the local
  Evidence Explorer makes assurance artifacts reviewable without uploading them.
  Version 0.10 adds an installable, one-command operational pilot that creates
  and independently verifies a cross-bound synthetic evidence bundle. Version
  0.11 adds LureWatch, an aggregate-only, anytime-valid post-deployment FPR/FNR
  monitor with hash-chained checkpoints and optional DSSE authentication.
version: 0.11.0
